# anima_art

Game art by Anima on our Forge: icons (flat / painted), portraits, UI elements — the pipeline in tools/anima and the lessons of the trials.

The full procedure is in [.claude/skills/anima_art/SKILL.md](mdc:.claude/skills/anima_art/SKILL.md).

Read that file when this rule triggers, then follow it.

**Quick reference:**

- `make_jobs.py` → `jobs/*.json`; `anima_gen.py` on the server (`--style painted` → `out_painted/`, `--recut`); `install.py` by `picks*.json` (`variant`, `redo`, `reseed`, `overlay` incl. `strike`, `same` — laid from another icon's pick)
- `--style painted` draws by BG3-like families (`FAMILY`, docs/design/ux/bg3-icons.md): items an object cut out, spells a bright glowing sign on a rounded stone tile cut out of black, features the same sign on a plate of bright steel, acts hands or a thing in a few dark ink strokes on that steel, traits the sign on bronze, conditions a flat emblem in a thin gold ring, ui thin gold outlines on black (cut by brightness, one gold), groups objects, marks flat; a tile is cut by its shape, an object at home by matte.py (BiRefNet on the GPU), never by colour
- `--style lines` (the author's trial of 2026-11-12, into `out_lines/`, picked into `picks_lines_icons.json`, the painted icons untouched): spells, features, acts and traits as the gold ui buttons in a frame — a spell in a gold ring with its sign in its school's colour, a feature and an act in a gold square, a trait in a silver one; the model draws only the sign in white lines (family `sign`), the frame, the colour (`tint` of a job: `schools` of game/data/icons.json, a subject's own `tint`) and the lines' width are laid by code (`lines`, `LINES`, `bolder`), changed by `--recut` with nothing drawn again; its acts by FLUX into `out_lines_flux/`; three variants each (`SEEDS`), the server draws spells, features and traits (1260 frames, ~6.7 h)
- `--backend openrouter` draws the same prompt by FLUX 3 Klein (no negative, the seed not kept) into `out_painted_flux/`, picked into `picks_flux.json`; the acts are drawn by it (2026-11-12)
- `pick.py` is one page for every kind drawn (`http://127.0.0.1:8791/`, a button per set, `#acts`, the lines style's `#lines_spells`…); each set writes into its folder's picks file (`SETS`: title, folder, picks file, the jobs' kind); the box «перерисовать» writes `redraw` (key → the author's note), `pick.py --marked` lists them
- A systematic miss (a tag like «wolf», «no humans», «small») is fixed in `subjects.json` / `portraits.json`, a random one by `reseed`; review at the game's size
- ControlNet LLLite breaks Forge on its second call: unload the checkpoint after each frame, never run it beside another job; never use another game's art as a reference
- Interface: `ui/guides.py` → `ui/paint.py` (a style in `STYLE`) → `ui/mock.py`, `ui/preview.py` (the game's screens of the picks, «Превью» in `pick.py`), `ui/frames.py` (the picks into `game/assets/ui/frames/` by `frames` of `game/data/icons.json`, laid by `UiTheme.skin`); the author's pick is the `lines` style (2026-11-12): a dark panel in two thin gold lines, ornaments only in the corners, crest / divider / ring laid whole on black
